WEBVTT

00:00:22.773 --> 00:00:24.650
It made it in time.

00:00:24.859 --> 00:00:26.694
It made it in time...

00:00:26.903 --> 00:00:30.031
There's only one thing left to do.

00:00:31.574 --> 00:00:33.367
Johann“.

00:00:33.576 --> 00:00:36.287
I'm doing what you wanted.

00:00:36.495 --> 00:00:38.039
No matter how...

00:00:38.247 --> 00:00:40.583
No matter how much I don't want to.

00:00:41.417 --> 00:00:44.045
But I will not move.

00:00:44.253 --> 00:00:47.381
Not until an impossible miracle occurs.

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:50.593
That is the only thing I can do

00:00:50.801 --> 00:00:52.762
to resist someone so dear.

00:01:12.448 --> 00:01:16.661
<i>This is me. My hair streams across...</i>

00:01:16.869 --> 00:01:21.249
<i>...my cheeks dyed red</i>

00:01:21.457 --> 00:01:25.419
<i>I am me... A grain of determination</i>

00:01:25.628 --> 00:01:30.174
<i>That was how it began</i>

00:01:30.383 --> 00:01:40.810
<i>If there is a tomorrow that is not
hazed over by hope or despair,</i>

00:01:41.018 --> 00:01:42.186
<i>(simple as that)</i>

00:01:42.395 --> 00:01:44.689
<i>I will not forget</i>

00:01:44.897 --> 00:01:50.236
<i>This pain is the promise we made that day</i>

00:01:50.444 --> 00:01:53.239
<i>I want to make it come true, I can't, I will</i>

00:01:53.447 --> 00:02:00.204
<i>At night I grab the void and awaken
to something in the morning</i>

00:02:00.413 --> 00:02:10.172
<i>I merely soar into the endless sky,
taking the shackles called "reason" Yes,</i>

00:02:10.381 --> 00:02:14.135
<i>"That is all.</i> "

00:02:35.031 --> 00:02:37.158
Preventing the revival
of the Creator God...

00:02:37.366 --> 00:02:39.035
Capturing the Palace of the Stars...

00:02:39.243 --> 00:02:41.287
Destroying the Ball Masque's leadership...

00:02:41.495 --> 00:02:44.040
We didn't accomplish any of them.

00:02:52.214 --> 00:02:53.424
I can see it!

00:02:53.632 --> 00:02:55.718
Hong Kong International Airport.

00:02:55.926 --> 00:02:58.929
We'll meet Sophie-san
and the others there...

00:03:05.978 --> 00:03:08.397
What's with you guys?

00:03:08.606 --> 00:03:10.733
Feels like we're at a funeral.

00:03:10.941 --> 00:03:14.236
Don't you want to celebrate our return--

00:03:14.445 --> 00:03:17.907
Have some consideration
for others, stupid Marco!

00:03:18.115 --> 00:03:19.867
I'm saying it out of consideration...

00:03:20.076 --> 00:03:23.245
Everyone looks so damned depressed.

00:03:24.246 --> 00:03:26.582
She must be tired, indeed.

00:03:26.791 --> 00:03:28.417
Rest needed.

00:03:44.683 --> 00:03:46.102
<i>Yo'.!</i>

00:03:46.477 --> 00:03:50.231
Yeah, I'm glad you
made it here as planned.

00:03:53.484 --> 00:03:54.360
Now, then...

00:03:54.568 --> 00:03:58.447
We got our asses kicked,
as the kids say.

00:04:03.828 --> 00:04:08.749
Jeez, that's a pretty nasty
rallying speech from our leader.

00:04:08.958 --> 00:04:10.835
But the expression applies.

00:04:11.043 --> 00:04:12.253
Got that right.

00:04:12.461 --> 00:04:13.337
Morale is at zero,

00:04:13.546 --> 00:04:16.173
and we've lost eighty percent of
our troops from that battle.

00:04:16.382 --> 00:04:18.634
Things are as bad as
the look on the old man's face.

00:04:18.843 --> 00:04:20.803
Yeah, his face aside,

00:04:21.011 --> 00:04:24.849
most people would say
we're finished as an army.

00:04:25.057 --> 00:04:27.726
But you seem
pretty cheerful, given all that.

00:04:27.935 --> 00:04:30.062
Do you have any counterattack plans?

00:04:31.647 --> 00:04:33.691
Not a one.

00:04:33.899 --> 00:04:39.071
But remember what we were told.

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:41.866
The words "to fight."

00:04:42.074 --> 00:04:43.075
Yes.

00:04:43.284 --> 00:04:45.119
It isn't over yet.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:53.210
We still have one card left to play.

00:05:00.384 --> 00:05:02.970
Those are my thoughts on the situation.

00:05:08.767 --> 00:05:10.811
I see...

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:13.856
I think it isn't a bad goal.

00:05:14.064 --> 00:05:17.359
It's like tossing a thread
through the eye of a needle.

00:05:17.568 --> 00:05:20.112
Isn't it just arrogance to
try two crazy plans in a row?

00:05:20.321 --> 00:05:22.072
But it's not impossible.

00:05:22.281 --> 00:05:26.202
We have the scroll of
secrets the Spiral Organ gave to

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:28.412
the Specialist of Everything.

00:05:32.166 --> 00:05:34.752
I can offer you two things.

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:37.546
The first is information.

00:05:37.755 --> 00:05:39.590
The other is...

00:05:40.591 --> 00:05:45.971
I don't agree with the
Creator God's optimism,

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:48.807
when he says that a new world
will mean no further need to fight.

00:05:49.016 --> 00:05:52.561
I say this because of the truth
that Centerhill revealed to us.

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:54.355
Damage to the world

00:05:54.563 --> 00:05:58.651
does not occur because the
Crimson Denizens use power of existence.

00:05:58.859 --> 00:06:00.069
It occurs because

00:06:00.277 --> 00:06:04.156
they eat humans, forcing the power
of existence into an unstable state.

00:06:04.365 --> 00:06:06.784
Presupposing, as he claims,

00:06:06.992 --> 00:06:09.745
all Denizens were
to leave for the new world...

00:06:09.954 --> 00:06:12.957
And that, as he says, the new world
overflows with power of existence...

00:06:13.165 --> 00:06:16.252
If they act there as they have here...

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:18.921
...everything will still happen again.

00:06:19.129 --> 00:06:23.676
This world may be safe for hundreds,
even thousands, of years.

00:06:23.884 --> 00:06:25.636
But in the distant future,

00:06:25.844 --> 00:06:28.806
the Crimson World,
this world, and the new world

00:06:29.014 --> 00:06:33.561
will be threatened by a great
disaster that cannot be averted.

00:06:33.769 --> 00:06:34.520
That's why I--

00:06:34.728 --> 00:06:35.938
Wait.

00:06:36.146 --> 00:06:40.526
You understand that we have
just suffered a great defeat, yes?

00:06:41.735 --> 00:06:42.611
Yeah.

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:44.697
That is why we're rushing to explain...

00:06:44.905 --> 00:06:46.740
I do not mean your plan.

00:06:46.949 --> 00:06:49.285
I'm referring to everyone's feelings.

00:06:50.494 --> 00:06:51.745
AS YOU Say!

00:06:51.954 --> 00:06:55.124
We could fight to protect the
balance of the world.

00:06:55.332 --> 00:06:58.168
That is our task as Flame Hazes.

00:06:59.295 --> 00:07:04.508
But I'm sure you know
that that is merely an excuse.

00:07:04.717 --> 00:07:08.637
That is why the words of the
Snake of the Festival, Yuji Sakai,

00:07:08.846 --> 00:07:11.473
were sufficient to send
the Flame Hazes running.

00:07:11.682 --> 00:07:16.645
Many Flame Hazes live to
execute personal oaths of vengeance.

00:07:16.854 --> 00:07:21.567
Forcing them to fight for a
world that isn't even ours is cruel.

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:25.738
Of course,

00:07:25.946 --> 00:07:29.700
everyone here is quite courageous.

00:07:29.908 --> 00:07:33.162
But I think that,
to decide our next course,

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:35.456
we should look inwards,

00:07:35.664 --> 00:07:38.334
rather than to your words.

00:07:39.585 --> 00:07:43.339
And HQ still has yet to reach a decision.

00:07:43.547 --> 00:07:47.259
Which means that any further
battles will be our own, private ones.

00:07:47.468 --> 00:07:51.180
I cannot guarantee we'll
receive any Outlaw support.

00:07:51.388 --> 00:07:52.973
Sounds good to me!

00:07:53.182 --> 00:07:55.559
Basically, we just
have to be ready for it, right?

00:07:55.768 --> 00:07:59.605
You just said that our
battles are ours alone, didn't you?

00:07:59.813 --> 00:08:00.689
No.

00:08:00.898 --> 00:08:05.319
As the commander said,
this is not a matter to decide lightly.

00:08:05.527 --> 00:08:09.490
It's not a battle you can
begin unless you're truly certain.

00:08:09.698 --> 00:08:13.410
But it's also true that we've little time.

00:08:13.619 --> 00:08:15.996
We have four hours until the charter flight,

00:08:16.205 --> 00:08:18.290
that Frangois has arranged, departs.

00:08:18.499 --> 00:08:23.712
Each of you, use that
time to consider everything.

00:08:23.921 --> 00:08:25.798
Each of you, decide what you will do.

00:08:26.006 --> 00:08:29.843
It is your choice
whether you return here.

00:08:36.809 --> 00:08:39.812
"To Battle, Once More"

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:45.943
She's been thinking this over,
all this time, indeed.

00:08:46.151 --> 00:08:47.986
Abrupt announcement.

00:08:48.195 --> 00:08:49.196
In other words,

00:08:49.405 --> 00:08:53.409
she's been considering our next
move ever since that enormous defeat.

00:08:55.494 --> 00:08:58.789
Foolishly, I thought her simply tired.

00:08:58.997 --> 00:09:00.791
Same opinion.

00:09:00.999 --> 00:09:03.001
Since she was little, I've told her...

00:09:04.086 --> 00:09:06.714
Fight for our cause.

00:09:06.922 --> 00:09:09.299
That is what a Flame Haze does.

00:09:10.676 --> 00:09:14.263
That is what I've been telling her.

00:09:14.471 --> 00:09:17.933
For the sake of a friend who
sacrificed herself to the cause.

00:09:21.311 --> 00:09:25.482
And now that the very
cause appears to waver,

00:09:25.691 --> 00:09:29.194
she herself is...

00:09:29.403 --> 00:09:31.780
It's not over yet.

00:09:31.989 --> 00:09:34.199
What gives her that toughness?

00:09:34.408 --> 00:09:36.243
Yuji Sakai.

00:09:47.588 --> 00:09:49.006
Margery-san!

00:09:51.550 --> 00:09:54.052
Hey, you made it, kid.

00:09:54.261 --> 00:09:55.512
How is the Palace of Heaven's Road?

00:09:55.721 --> 00:09:58.974
Frangois-san has it
moored outside the city.

00:09:59.183 --> 00:10:01.602
It'd be dangerous
to have it near the airport.

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:03.187
That's good.

00:10:03.395 --> 00:10:06.273
Shana-chan told me what happened.

00:10:06.482 --> 00:10:08.901
Margery-san, what are you going to do?

00:10:10.444 --> 00:10:12.196
Go with her?

00:10:13.614 --> 00:10:15.741
You're still asking me that?

00:10:15.949 --> 00:10:17.618
Well...

00:10:17.826 --> 00:10:21.830
I lost any devotion to the cause
or to revenge a long time ago.

00:10:22.039 --> 00:10:24.958
I didn't need to hear that ass speak.

00:10:25.167 --> 00:10:26.335
Then“.

00:10:26.543 --> 00:10:28.420
Balar would say

00:10:28.629 --> 00:10:31.715
that I'm already in this,
and it's too late to back out.

00:10:31.924 --> 00:10:36.929
After coming all this way,
all that's left is finishing the job.

00:10:37.971 --> 00:10:39.515
Keisaku, what about you?

00:10:39.723 --> 00:10:42.851
I decided a long time ago, too.

00:10:43.060 --> 00:10:45.312
I'll go with you, Margery-san.

00:10:45.521 --> 00:10:47.147
Arrogant boy.

00:10:52.569 --> 00:10:55.155
I hope that girl's safe.

00:10:55.364 --> 00:10:57.616
Yeah, I do, too.

00:10:58.659 --> 00:11:03.413
So you guys are gonna
have someone to fight for now?

00:11:03.622 --> 00:11:04.540
Yeah.

00:11:04.748 --> 00:11:08.710
Looking at you, I assume we
needn't ask what your decision is.

00:11:08.919 --> 00:11:12.589
Thanks to a certain someone,
my contractor is all fired up.

00:11:12.798 --> 00:11:14.925
I wouldn't say fired up.

00:11:15.133 --> 00:11:19.763
But I have some pride
invested in the vow I took.

00:11:19.972 --> 00:11:23.058
Indeed, I understand that.

00:11:23.267 --> 00:11:24.560
Part of it is just

00:11:24.768 --> 00:11:28.355
my instinct that if something sounds
too good to be true, it probably is.

00:11:28.564 --> 00:11:30.899
Especially considering the source.

00:11:31.108 --> 00:11:33.443
Me aside, what about you two?

00:11:33.652 --> 00:11:34.528
Yeah.

00:11:34.736 --> 00:11:39.408
If her plan is the one
most likely to get results,

00:11:39.616 --> 00:11:41.577
then we should try it.

00:11:42.536 --> 00:11:44.121
I can understand that.

00:11:44.329 --> 00:11:49.751
Indeed, but we lack
the numbers for it.

00:11:49.960 --> 00:11:53.672
Well, let's start by praying
we don't lose any more.

00:11:57.801 --> 00:11:59.011
Sale-san,

00:11:59.219 --> 00:12:03.849
I think Shana-san's
plan will be best for everyone.

00:12:04.057 --> 00:12:06.435
We were told to
decide for ourselves, right?

00:12:06.643 --> 00:12:08.186
You don't need my agreement.

00:12:08.395 --> 00:12:11.607
Jeez, you really are dense.

00:12:11.815 --> 00:12:14.192
Don't you realize that she's worried

00:12:14.401 --> 00:12:17.571
you'll choose a
different path than she does?

00:12:17.779 --> 00:12:21.199
No... I've already decided.

00:12:21.408 --> 00:12:23.535
Her plan seems fun.

00:12:23.744 --> 00:12:26.705
I guess that's what you'd expect from
the God of Atonement's contractor.

00:12:26.914 --> 00:12:32.336
I've heard this "change the world"
stuff before, so I'm interested.

00:12:33.921 --> 00:12:37.132
I'm an exception, someone
who isn't motivated by revenge.

00:12:37.341 --> 00:12:39.718
I'm an artificially created Flame Haze.

00:12:41.303 --> 00:12:44.765
And my creator is involved in this.

00:12:44.973 --> 00:12:49.144
I'll stop him from going to a world
suffused with power of existence.

00:12:49.353 --> 00:12:52.314
That's more than reason enough to fight.

00:13:00.030 --> 00:13:02.199
Hurry UP!

00:13:02.407 --> 00:13:06.578
You can get the Crypta up later.

00:13:06.787 --> 00:13:08.497
Right now,

00:13:08.705 --> 00:13:14.086
our goal is to get the Palace of the Stars

00:13:14.294 --> 00:13:16.505
back up and flying!

00:13:16.713 --> 00:13:20.175
But without the Crypta, the Palace
of the Stars will be plainly visible.

00:13:20.384 --> 00:13:24.763
Domino, I know that!

00:13:24.972 --> 00:13:30.686
But our first priority is to keep
the Outlaws from having time to plan!

00:13:30.894 --> 00:13:33.939
That was Bel-Peel's order,

00:13:34.147 --> 00:13:36.775
and it still stands!

00:13:36.984 --> 00:13:40.278
So, you have another
declaration for the Denizens?

00:13:40.487 --> 00:13:41.405
Yes.

00:13:41.613 --> 00:13:45.867
We shall perform the ceremony to
create the paradise Xanadu, in Japan.

00:13:46.076 --> 00:13:47.494
That is all I'll say.

00:13:47.703 --> 00:13:50.622
That's a rather vague declaration.

00:13:50.831 --> 00:13:52.374
That's enough for now.

00:13:52.582 --> 00:13:54.084
Yes, Sir.

00:14:01.883 --> 00:14:04.386
You'll perform the creation ceremony here?

00:14:04.594 --> 00:14:06.847
It must be here.

00:14:07.055 --> 00:14:09.975
I'd like your help in this,

00:14:10.183 --> 00:14:11.810
Spiral Organ.

00:14:12.019 --> 00:14:13.228
Will it involve

00:14:13.437 --> 00:14:17.065
something beyond the task
I've already been hired for?

00:14:17.274 --> 00:14:18.483
Yes.

00:14:19.693 --> 00:14:21.528
That is...

00:14:21.737 --> 00:14:23.905
It belonged to the Hunter, Friagne.

00:14:24.114 --> 00:14:26.324
Yes. What of it?

00:14:26.533 --> 00:14:27.617
Nothing.

00:14:27.826 --> 00:14:32.247
I was merely thinking
that fate is sometimes strange.

00:14:32.456 --> 00:14:34.750
Thank you, Sophie Sawallisch.

00:14:34.958 --> 00:14:36.793
For what?

00:14:37.002 --> 00:14:39.713
I was thinking only of my own task.

00:14:39.921 --> 00:14:42.507
I wasn't considering everyone else.

00:14:42.716 --> 00:14:46.887
Caught up in her
enthusiasm, I was careless.

00:14:47.095 --> 00:14:48.555
I apologize.

00:14:49.723 --> 00:14:51.933
Whether anyone agrees or not,

00:14:52.142 --> 00:14:55.062
you're taking the lead down a new path.

00:14:55.270 --> 00:14:58.356
I think that's much better than being frail.

00:15:03.570 --> 00:15:05.697
They have them in Hong Kong, too!

00:15:05.906 --> 00:15:07.324
My! my...

00:15:11.912 --> 00:15:14.581
Your smile hasn't changed.

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:17.501
It tastes a little different
than the Japanese kind.

00:15:17.709 --> 00:15:20.712
But the outside's crispy,
and the inside's fluffy.

00:15:20.921 --> 00:15:23.965
--Do you think our helpful
advice was really needed,

00:15:23.965 --> 00:15:26.301
--It's delicious! --Do you think our
helpful advice was really needed,

00:15:26.510 --> 00:15:28.136
Sophie Sawallisch-kun?

00:15:28.345 --> 00:15:29.429
Let me see.

00:15:29.638 --> 00:15:31.431
If nothing else,

00:15:31.640 --> 00:15:36.478
it gave me the courage to carry out
what we're about to do, Takemikazuchi.

00:15:36.686 --> 00:15:39.272
That's right. There's no need to worry.

00:15:40.607 --> 00:15:44.319
You are solely yourself,
without further deception.

00:15:44.528 --> 00:15:45.946
Right?

00:15:46.696 --> 00:15:48.115
Yeah.

00:15:49.866 --> 00:15:53.870
Yuji, I'm sure you also...

00:15:54.079 --> 00:15:59.584
Now I can return to Zurich
headquarters without worry, right?

00:15:59.793 --> 00:16:01.253
To headquarters?

00:16:01.461 --> 00:16:04.047
They have demanded her presence there.

00:16:04.256 --> 00:16:07.425
For an emergency meeting,
to discuss this defeat.

00:16:07.634 --> 00:16:09.469
The meeting is just a pretext.

00:16:09.678 --> 00:16:13.348
If you go, they'll simply
pin all the blame on you.

00:16:13.557 --> 00:16:14.724
It's possible that...

00:16:14.933 --> 00:16:17.144
I will probably be
released from command.

00:16:17.352 --> 00:16:18.186
Sophie!

00:16:18.395 --> 00:16:23.859
Part of my job as commander is
taking responsibility for failures.

00:16:25.235 --> 00:16:27.821
Come... It's almost time.

00:16:28.029 --> 00:16:29.114
As I see it,

00:16:29.322 --> 00:16:32.534
none of the Flame Hazes
are sensible enough

00:16:32.742 --> 00:16:34.161
to drop out here.

00:16:34.369 --> 00:16:35.328
Yeah.

00:16:35.537 --> 00:16:38.498
I'll be taking a
special flight back tonight.

00:16:38.707 --> 00:16:42.586
I took a long vacation, so for once,
we'll have some time together.

00:16:42.794 --> 00:16:44.754
But it's a shame...

00:16:44.963 --> 00:16:48.383
Carmel-san and Shana-chan
haven't been back for a while.

00:16:48.592 --> 00:16:51.428
I see... That's too bad.

00:16:51.636 --> 00:16:54.014
Well, then I'll be able
to spend some time with you.

00:16:54.222 --> 00:16:57.309
And with the newest member of the family.

00:16:57.517 --> 00:17:02.105
I can take good care of my wife,
since I don't usually get the chance.

00:17:02.314 --> 00:17:04.774
Okay. I'm looking forward to it.

00:17:15.202 --> 00:17:17.579
It seems everyone has decided, indeed.

00:17:17.787 --> 00:17:19.915
Even if all their reasons differ...

00:17:20.123 --> 00:17:21.583
Unwavering determination.

00:17:21.791 --> 00:17:23.251
With the emotions in their hearts,

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:27.964
everyone will move
forward as best they can.

00:17:28.173 --> 00:17:30.884
I've been living as
hard as I can for a long time.

00:17:31.092 --> 00:17:34.179
That's right, isn't it,

00:17:34.387 --> 00:17:36.014
Mathilde Saint-Omar?

00:17:37.849 --> 00:17:38.975
The child that l...

00:17:39.184 --> 00:17:41.478
That we raised...

00:17:41.686 --> 00:17:44.981
She'll follow the path she's decided on.

00:17:45.190 --> 00:17:47.651
Let us fight for that.

00:18:07.921 --> 00:18:11.383
So they'll be making
that paradise in Japan, huh?

00:18:13.718 --> 00:18:17.764
I got a request for help,
from Ball Masque yesterday.

00:18:17.973 --> 00:18:20.475
Who knows how they found us...

00:18:20.684 --> 00:18:25.897
Well, I'm sure they want all
the pawns they can get to help.

00:18:26.106 --> 00:18:30.568
I like using others as
pawns, but not being used.

00:18:30.777 --> 00:18:32.320
I know that.

00:18:32.529 --> 00:18:36.408
But are you sure you
want to ignore this, boss?

00:18:36.616 --> 00:18:39.369
I don't give a crap about gods or Xanadu.

00:18:39.577 --> 00:18:42.706
Paradise isn't something
you strain yourself over.

00:18:42.914 --> 00:18:47.502
I'm satisfied with gentle sunlight and
a cup of coffee with friendly neighbors.

00:18:47.711 --> 00:18:50.088
We're cheap, relaxed, and simple.

00:18:50.297 --> 00:18:53.008
We have no need for gods.

00:18:55.552 --> 00:18:57.178
You have a letter.

00:18:58.305 --> 00:18:59.556
Thank you, Louie.

00:18:59.764 --> 00:19:01.182
Here you go.

00:19:04.853 --> 00:19:07.022
I found you.

00:19:07.230 --> 00:19:09.858
I wish I hadn't.

00:19:27.125 --> 00:19:31.755
Everyone, fight as
you will, as hard as you can.

00:19:31.963 --> 00:19:34.799
We'll be getting a lecture in Zurich,

00:19:35.008 --> 00:19:36.676
so do some damage for us, too.

00:19:36.885 --> 00:19:38.928
You can count on me.

00:19:39.137 --> 00:19:43.475
I'll just act natural and get inside
the Palace of Heaven's Road.

00:19:43.683 --> 00:19:48.271
Give us the exact timing,
once the plan's schedule is decided.

00:19:48.480 --> 00:19:51.775
Tell Frangois I said hello.

00:19:56.696 --> 00:19:59.532
It'll be a forced march from here on out.

00:19:59.741 --> 00:20:02.577
First, we'll cross
the Pacific and then return.

00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:07.874
I hope we'll have three more
when we come back, though.

00:20:08.083 --> 00:20:09.459
I've arranged a meeting.

00:20:09.667 --> 00:20:14.464
The remaining Gods of the Earth
await you in New York, indeed.

00:20:14.672 --> 00:20:17.592
Yeah, with their help,

00:20:17.801 --> 00:20:20.595
things will be much easier.

00:20:20.804 --> 00:20:26.101
Indeed. But whether
they'll agree to fight with us...

00:20:26.309 --> 00:20:27.894
Difficult battle.

00:20:28.103 --> 00:20:29.896
Worrying won't help.

00:20:30.105 --> 00:20:32.315
We'll talk with them first.

00:20:32.524 --> 00:20:33.775
That's right.

00:20:33.983 --> 00:20:36.236
Especially in their case...

00:20:36.444 --> 00:20:38.863
They're good people, but...

00:20:39.072 --> 00:20:43.076
But the fact that Centerhill is the
easiest to deal with tells you something.

00:20:43.284 --> 00:20:45.537
I don't look forward to it,
but there's no choice, huh?

00:20:45.745 --> 00:20:48.748
Yes... To New York.

00:20:48.957 --> 00:20:51.376
I'll tell the remaining Gods of the Earth

00:20:51.584 --> 00:20:54.254
the words that Centerhill left behind.

00:21:11.688 --> 00:21:15.024
<i>The moon and stars
are illuminating me</i>

00:21:15.233 --> 00:21:18.528
<i>On top of the carpet with dancing sparks</i>

00:21:18.736 --> 00:21:22.198
<i>You are right in front of me,
glowing red in the light</i>

00:21:22.407 --> 00:21:25.827
<i>Your honest eyes are twinkling</i>

00:21:26.035 --> 00:21:29.581
<i>The two footsteps, they head
toward the distant yonder</i>

00:21:29.581 --> 00:21:30.206
Restart successful!

00:21:30.206 --> 00:21:34.502
<i>The words I told you said,
"Let's leave everything behind"</i>

00:21:34.711 --> 00:21:39.841
<i>Fly toward the future</i>

00:21:40.049 --> 00:21:44.345
<i>The motive has a strong grasp on
my heart Yes, this is the ultimate descent</i>

00:21:44.554 --> 00:21:48.016
<i>The two of us are fellow soldiers
flattering one another's pulses</i>

00:21:48.016 --> 00:21:49.142
To Misaki City.

00:21:49.142 --> 00:21:51.394
<i>H' you are going to protect
your love, you cannot reject battle</i>

00:21:51.603 --> 00:21:55.106
<i>Without fudging a phrase,
we rhyme down this hot path</i>

00:21:55.106 --> 00:21:55.398
I'll find you and...

00:21:55.398 --> 00:21:58.359
<i>Passing each other by, quarreling</i>

00:21:58.568 --> 00:22:02.113
<i>Set free from the enchantment</i>

00:22:02.322 --> 00:22:05.658
<i>If you are going to leave on a journey,</i>

00:22:05.867 --> 00:22:09.496
<i>I will never let go of your hand again</i>

00:22:09.704 --> 00:22:12.957
<i>Do you still remember the first time</i>

00:22:13.166 --> 00:22:16.711
<i>Our eyes locked, just as it happened?</i>

00:22:16.920 --> 00:22:19.964
<i>Even if I am engulfed
by the vortex of slumber,</i>

00:22:20.173 --> 00:22:25.929
<i>It will not vanish,
I won't let it--It's our dream</i>

00:22:26.137 --> 00:22:27.347
<i>To be as ONE</i>

00:22:27.555 --> 00:22:31.434
<i>With an unfaltering voice, you make sure</i>

00:22:31.643 --> 00:22:34.562
<i>To keep the tiny scrap of
paper from burning asunder</i>

00:22:34.771 --> 00:22:38.733
<i>I won't forget about you,
even if my body vanishes</i>

00:22:38.942 --> 00:22:42.153
<i>I will remember how we lived together</i>

00:22:42.362 --> 00:22:45.698
<i>Snow of light flutters down the sky</i>

00:22:45.907 --> 00:22:49.536
<i>Where the waning moon
and stars go to snuggle</i>

00:22:49.744 --> 00:22:52.705
<i>The story we are writing</i>

00:22:52.914 --> 00:22:56.376
<i>Will continue on even
after this, for all eternity</i>

00:22:56.584 --> 00:23:00.630
<i>The motive has a strong grasp on
my heart Yes, this is the ultimate descent</i>

00:23:00.838 --> 00:23:04.509
<i>The two of us are fellow soldiers
flattering one another's pulses</i>

00:23:04.717 --> 00:23:07.720
<i>If you are going to protect your love,
you cannot reject battle</i>

00:23:07.929 --> 00:23:13.184
<i>Without fudging a phrase, we rhyme
as we travel down overlapping paths</i>

00:23:13.393 --> 00:23:19.857
<i>The moment we discovered the conclusion,
time merely continued to move on</i>

00:23:20.066 --> 00:23:23.528
<i>As the snow of light flurries down</i>

00:23:26.990 --> 00:23:28.658
Shana and the others head to New York,

00:23:28.866 --> 00:23:31.494
to ask for the
Three Gods of the Earth's help.

00:23:31.703 --> 00:23:32.870
Meanwhile, in Misaki City,

00:23:33.079 --> 00:23:36.958
Yuji appears once more
before Yoshida and Tanaka.

00:23:37.166 --> 00:23:39.294
Next time,
on Shakugan no Shana Final:

00:23:39.502 --> 00:23:40.837
"For Whose Sake?"
